WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Strategic Foundations
Recap: Strategic Foundations

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your Strategic Foundation is one connected set of decisions. Read it as a whole.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
You made the connected decisions everything else rests on: why your initiative should exist, its context and people, your values and form, where you add unique value and what comes first.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:37.030
1.1 Purpose, vision and mission: Purpose: why you exist. Vision: the future you seek. Mission: what you do, for whom and how.

6
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:47.148
1.2 Context and landscape analysis: Who has the problem, how they cope today and what is changing show where your idea can fit.

7
00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:57.526
1.3 Stakeholder mapping: Mapping who affects or is affected by your work shows whom to involve, and how, before you launch.

8
00:00:57.926 --> 00:00:58.526
One lesson at a time

9
00:00:58.526 --> 00:01:07.904
1.4 Values in practice: A value only guides you when it describes what people will actually do, especially in hard decisions.

10
00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:17.281
1.5 Organisational form and identity: Your legal form is the vehicle for your mission; staying informal for now can be valid.

11
00:01:17.281 --> 00:01:26.548
1.6 Positioning and comparative advantage: Positioning answers one question: why you, rather than someone else, or no one?

12
00:01:26.948 --> 00:01:27.548
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:27.548 --> 00:01:38.296
1.7 Strategic objectives: external and internal: A few strategic objectives, external and internal, turn your mission into priorities; the rest can wait.

14
00:01:38.896 --> 00:01:51.496
Your Theory of Change builds one pathway for each external objective, and later modules use your values, form and priorities to organise, prove and protect the work.

15
00:01:52.096 --> 00:01:56.896
You check your Strategic Foundation and download each exercise as a PDF.

16
00:01:58.396 --> 00:02:01.496
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
